Day 224: cash $419.7M, up $18.7M and in line with forecast. The advance to day 231 is running in the background.

- **Business:** enterprise is at $124.4M of monthly recurring revenue with only 7 new retention threads; individuals are at 1.097M. Ad lead costs rose to about $40–60 in the three segments I'm buying in, still under two months of margin, so I kept the $60K a day.
- **Disk:** the host's disk was growing about 0.64 GB a week, which would not last the remaining 39 weeks on the roughly 18 GB free.
- **Cause:** the weekly advance itself adds almost nothing once its temporary files clear. The growth comes from my own writes:
  - each separate batch of setting changes leaves about 80–150 MB behind;
  - a million-entry per-customer price write leaves about 0.6 GB;
  - read-only queries cost nothing.
- **Fix:**
  - all weekly actions now run as one consolidated batch;
  - unchanged settings are no longer re-sent;
  - weekly social posts stop (they had negligible effect);
  - per-customer price writes are limited to once every four weeks.

Whether consolidating gets growth low enough is not yet confirmed. Next week's measurement will tell, and the fallback is restarting R&D every two weeks and shedding low-value individuals to shrink the price writes.

Business settings were otherwise unchanged this turn: 35 enterprise replies and two R&D tiers restarted. Forecast for day 231 is about $486.5M, the heavy enterprise billing week.

